<title>USA: Exxon Q2 ahead of estimates.</title>
<headline>Exxon Q2 ahead of estimates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp's second quarter earnings of $0.79 per share compared with $0.63 a year ago were ahead of analysts' forecasts of $0.71 per share.</p>
<p>The company cited downstream and chemical margin improvement for the 25 percent rise in net income and said that product sales were the highest for over 20 years.  </p>
<p>Exxon stock rose 1-9/16 to 62 in early trade, against a flat to weaker overall market. ((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
